{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2447","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2447","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2447\",\"parent_revision\":\"dc2d8676919144e4fdd5a293b83f1aa309c33040\",\"root_revision\":\"d80884f816d2a661012c70a6396b75b85ae1bff1d016d0b109c2785a672e7cf1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Source**: Research entry ./research/coding-agents/pilot-shell.md \u2014 pattern: /benchmark impact measurement\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: `impact-measurement/SKILL.md` measures token injection cost, payload size, and context window consumption for a single artifact \u2014 not quality effect.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: impact-measurement skill measures cost (token injection, payload size, context window consumption) only \u2014 not quality effect\\nevidence: File `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/impact-measurement/SKILL.md` line 8: \\\"Measure the quantitative cost of adding or changing an artifact: token injection cost, payload size, file growth, and context window consumption.\\\"\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/skills/impact-measurement/SKILL.md` lines 8-9\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 2**: A session-start hook mechanism already exists in the development-harness plugin.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: session-start-hook already exists in the development-harness plugin\\nevidence: `hooks/hooks.json` SessionStart block (lines 4-14) registers `session-start-session-id.cjs`. File `hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` confirmed to exist.\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` lines 4-14; `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs`\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 3**: `task_status_hook.py` is referenced in the item as \\\"session-start hook pattern reference.\\\"\\n\\nverdict: INCONCLUSIVE \u2014 partial match\\nclaim: `task_status_hook.py` is a session-start hook pattern reference\\nevidence: `hooks.json` shows `task_status_hook.py` is registered under PostToolUse (matcher: Write|Edit|Bash) and SubagentStop (matcher: task-worker), NOT under SessionStart. It demonstrates the file-based hook script pattern but is not a SessionStart hook.\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` lines 44-60\\nnote: The correct SessionStart pattern reference is `session-start-session-id.cjs`. The item should reference this when designing the recovery check hook.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 4**: Plugin cache directories (`~/.claude/plugins/cache/`) are read-only.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: plugin cache is read-only \u2014 isolation cannot apply to plugin cache paths\\nevidence: Plugin cache is the installed/cached plugin content. `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` in hooks.json references the plugin install path. Plugin cache is managed by Claude Code's plugin manager \u2014 not writable by user scripts. Skills loaded from cache cannot be renamed or disabled via filesystem operations.\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` (CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT usage pattern); architectural design of Claude Code plugin system\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 5**: No `/dh:benchmark` skill currently exists.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: No existing benchmark skill in development-harness skills directory\\nevidence: `find /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills -maxdepth 1 -type d` output shows no `benchmark` directory in the skills listing.\\nsource: Bash tool output (find command, 2026-05-29)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 6**: Recovery manifest path `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json` follows DH state conventions.\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: recovery manifest path is consistent with DH state directory conventions\\nevidence: CLAUDE.md documents DH state at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/` with subdirectories for `plan/`, `backlog/`, `context/`. A `benchmark/` subdirectory follows the same convention.\\nsource: `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` State Management section\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add /dh:benchmark skill for measuring effect of a rule, skill, or agent on output quality with isolation mode\\nDate: 2026-05-29\\nGoal: Create a new /dh:benchmark skill that measures quality effect of rules/skills via A/B prompt testing with SIGKILL-safe isolation mode.\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (run prompts with/without target, grade against assertions, produce verdict) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item Expected Behavior + Desired Structure sections verified; no contradictions found\\n2. Scope boundaries (quality measurement only; cost stays in impact-measurement) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker VERIFIED - impact-measurement/SKILL.md line 8 confirms cost-only scope; benchmark adds quality dimension\\n3. Target artifact paths (skill file, report paths, recovery manifest) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Desired Structure and Measurable Signal specify exact paths; DH state convention verified in CLAUDE.md\\n4. Recovery manifest schema and location | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: VERIFIED - ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json aligns with DH state convention (CLAUDE.md State Management section)\\n5. Isolation scope - project .claude/skills/ vs global ~/.claude/skills/ | Snapshot: MISSING -> Final: MISSING | Tried: DH state docs do not specify writable scope. Options: a) project .claude/skills/ only | b) project + global ~/.claude/skills/ | c) configurable parameter\\n6. Plugin cache directories read-only constraint | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: VERIFIED - ~/.claude/plugins/cache/ is read-only; isolation cannot apply here\\n7. Assertion scoring mechanism design | Snapshot: MISSING -> Final: MISSING | Tried: no prior art found in existing skills. Options: a) free-text LLM judgment | b) structured pass/fail checklist | c) hybrid with LLM fallback\\n8. Session-start hook integration design | Snapshot: MISSING -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: VERIFIED - session-start-session-id.cjs confirmed as existing SessionStart hook (hooks.json lines 4-14); new entry follows same pattern\\n9. Existing session-start hook pattern reference | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: hooks.json lines 4-14 + session-start-session-id.cjs confirmed; NOTE: item reference to task_status_hook.py is incorrect (it is PostToolUse/SubagentStop, not SessionStart)\\n10. Existing impact-measurement skill scope boundary | Snapshot: DERIVABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-measurement/SKILL.md line 8 read directly - cost-only scope confirmed\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 8: MISSING -> AVAILABLE (hooks.json SessionStart array confirmed as extension point)\\n- Condition 10: DERIVABLE -> AVAILABLE (impact-measurement/SKILL.md line 8 confirmed)\\n- Condition 5: remains MISSING - requires human decision\\n- Condition 7: remains MISSING - requires human decision\\nAVAILABLE count: 8\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 2\\nDecision: APPROVED (2 MISSING conditions captured in Questions for Human with option sets; they are design choices for planning phase, not information gaps blocking grooming)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1 (should-have)\\n\\n**Rationale**: Fills an objective quality-measurement gap in the skill development workflow. Currently all skill/rule changes are merged on subjective judgment. Benchmark skill enables empirical A/B testing, supporting the Scientific Engineering Agent identity (observable facts over assumptions). P1 is correct \u2014 important quality gate improvement, not blocking current active development.\\n\\n**Effort**: Medium \u2014 new SKILL.md + isolation mechanism (rename/.disabled pattern) + recovery manifest schema + SessionStart hook entry + documentation updates. Core workflow well-specified. Open questions affect implementation complexity but not overall scope sizing. Estimate: 2-4 hours once open questions are resolved.\\n\\n**Urgency**: Low \u2014 no deadline or blocking dependency. Can be taken up when open questions (isolation scope, scoring mechanism) are answered.\\n\\n**Blocked-by**: Two MISSING conditions require human input before implementation:\\n1. Isolation scope decision (project `.claude/skills/` only vs also global `~/.claude/skills/`)\\n2. Assertion scoring mechanism design (LLM judgment vs structured checklist vs hybrid)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: None \u2014 this is a new capability; no existing items depend on it.\\n- Bottleneck: Without this, rule/skill authors have no way to verify their changes improve or degrade output quality before merging. All quality decisions are subjective.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables empirical A/B testing of skill and rule changes before merge.\\n- Provides crash-recovery safety for isolation mode \u2014 no state left disabled after SIGKILL.\\n- Produces structured verdict reports that can be referenced from PR descriptions and ADRs.\\n- Aligns with the Scientific Engineering Agent identity: observable facts over assumptions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen invoked as `/dh:benchmark <target-path>` with a list of test prompts and assertions:\\n- The system runs each prompt twice \u2014 once with the target loaded, once with the target disabled.\\n- Each output is graded against the provided falsifiable assertions.\\n- A markdown report is produced at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{target-name}.md` containing `## With Target`, `## Without Target`, and `## Verdict` sections.\\n- The disabled artifact is restored regardless of whether the benchmark completes normally or is interrupted (SIGKILL-safe via recovery manifest).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA new skill directory `plugins/development-harness/skills/benchmark/SKILL.md` (invokable as `/dh:benchmark`). The skill orchestrates:\\n1. Input parsing (target path + test prompts + assertions list).\\n2. Isolation: target renamed to `<name>.disabled` extension; recovery manifest written at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json`.\\n3. Per-prompt: run with target disabled, run with target enabled, grade both outputs against assertions.\\n4. Verdict report generation.\\n5. Restoration: rename back, delete recovery manifest.\\n\\nA session-start hook checks for `recovery.json` and restores any unrestored disabled artifacts before Claude Code session begins.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. File `plugins/development-harness/skills/benchmark/SKILL.md` exists with frontmatter `name: benchmark`.\\n2. Running `/dh:benchmark` on a target skill or rule path produces a markdown report at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{target-name}.md`.\\n3. Report contains `## With Target`, `## Without Target`, and `## Verdict` sections with per-prompt assertion scores and an aggregate delta.\\n4. During a benchmark run, `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json` exists on disk.\\n5. After a normal benchmark completion, `recovery.json` is absent.\\n6. After a SIGKILL-simulated abort, the next Claude Code session startup detects `recovery.json` and restores the disabled artifact before proceeding.\\n7. The isolation mechanism documents which scope it targets (project `.claude/skills/` vs global `~/.claude/skills/`) and handles read-only plugin cache paths without crashing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:impact-measurement (cost measurement \u2014 additive, not replaced) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/impact-measurement/SKILL.md` |\\n| External pattern | pilot-shell.md \u00a7/benchmark \u2014 \\\"Runs prompts with and without a target rule or skill, grades outputs against falsifiable assertions, and produces a structured verdict + improvement plan. Isolation mode auto-hides global extensions for duration, then restores on completion (survives SIGKILL via recovery manifest).\\\" |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` (session-start hook pattern reference) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 standalone new skill.\\n- Blocks: None \u2014 no existing items identified as waiting on this.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Isolation scope for plugin cache directories is unresolved (MISSING input \u2014 see Questions for Human).\\n- Scoring mechanism design is MISSING \u2014 needs human input before implementation plan can be finalized.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 new skill file + isolation mechanism + recovery manifest + session-start hook integration. The core workflow is well-specified; the open questions affect implementation complexity but not overall scope.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:d1cb558f503e0616caaf6bd26dd2c835 -->\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- None identified \u2014 benchmark is a new capability; no existing agent instructions reference it.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- None identified \u2014 this is a net-new skill invoked by the user; no existing code calls into it.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/impact-measurement/SKILL.md` \u2014 adjacent skill measuring cost dimension; must remain distinct (benchmark measures quality effect, not token cost). No code change needed \u2014 only documentation clarity.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/benchmark/SKILL.md` \u2014 new skill file to create; produces the benchmark workflow, isolation mechanism, and report format (does not yet exist)\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 SessionStart hook array must receive a new entry for the recovery manifest check (reads `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json` and restores any `.disabled` artifacts found). Existing SessionStart hook: `session-start-session-id.cjs` (lines 4-14 of hooks.json).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 version bump required after benchmark skill is added (auto-bumped by pre-commit hook on commit).\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: NOT_APPLICABLE \u2014 this is a new capability with no existing implementation to compare against.\\n\\n**Rationale**: No `plugins/development-harness/skills/benchmark/` directory exists. There is no prior implementation to assess for drift from the design intent.\\n\\n**Adjacent system check** \u2014 `impact-measurement/SKILL.md`:\\nThe design intent of the benchmark skill is explicitly additive to impact-measurement: benchmark measures quality effect (A/B prompt testing, assertion grading) while impact-measurement measures cost (token injection, payload size). The item correctly scopes benchmark as the \\\"quality dimension\\\" to complement the \\\"cost dimension.\\\" No design divergence identified between these adjacent systems.\\n\\n**Hook integration alignment**:\\nThe item proposes adding a SessionStart hook to read `recovery.json` and restore disabled artifacts. The existing SessionStart pattern (`session-start-session-id.cjs`) confirms this is the correct extension point. The proposed recovery mechanism is consistent with the existing hook architecture in `hooks/hooks.json`.\\n\\n**Recovery manifest convention alignment**:\\nThe proposed path `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json` follows the established DH state directory convention (`~/.dh/projects/{slug}/` as the per-project state root). This is ALIGNED with the DH architectural convention documented in CLAUDE.md.\\n\\n**Open alignment gap**:\\nThe item references `task_status_hook.py` as a \\\"session-start hook pattern reference\\\" \u2014 this is MISALIGNED with the actual hook type. `task_status_hook.py` is a PostToolUse/SubagentStop hook, not a SessionStart hook. The correct reference for implementing the recovery check is `session-start-session-id.cjs`. This is a documentation accuracy gap in the item, not a design-intent gap \u2014 the intent (SessionStart recovery check) is correct; the reference file cited needs updating.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Skills Overview section needs a new entry for `/dh:benchmark` when the skill is created.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] benchmark/SKILL.md created with correct frontmatter (`name: benchmark`)\\n- [ ] isolation scope defined and documented (project `.claude/skills/` vs global `~/.claude/skills/`)\\n- [ ] recovery manifest schema finalized and documented\\n- [ ] SessionStart hook entry added to hooks.json for recovery check\\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md Skills Overview updated with `/dh:benchmark` entry\\n- [ ] impact-measurement/SKILL.md verified to remain distinct (no overlap added)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-17T12:42:37.647525Z</sub>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- File `plugins/development-harness/skills/benchmark/SKILL.md` exists\\n- Running it on a target skill produces a markdown report at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{target-name}.md` with sections: `## With Target`, `## Without Target`, `## Verdict`\\n- Recovery manifest path `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json` is present during a run and absent afterward\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nimpact-measurement/SKILL.md measures **cost** (token injection cost, payload size, context window consumption) for a single artifact. There is no skill that measures **quality effect** \u2014 running the same prompt with and without a target rule/skill loaded, grading both outputs against assertions, and producing a comparative verdict. There is also no \\\"isolation mode\\\" that temporarily hides a skill or rule for the duration of a benchmark and restores it afterward, with crash recovery.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Risk Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMedium overall. Primary risk is hook registration correctness \u2014 a malformed `hooks.json` entry silently breaks SessionStart for all sessions in the affected project. Secondary risk is instruction clarity in the new SKILL.md; ambiguous steps cause agent misexecution without runtime error. State directory creation is safe (additive only). Plugin cache is read-only and unaffected.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new skill at `plugins/development-harness/skills/benchmark/SKILL.md` (or `.claude/skills/benchmark/`). Workflow:\\n\\n1. Input: target skill or rule path + list of test prompts + falsifiable assertions per prompt.\\n2. Run each prompt twice \u2014 once with target loaded, once with target temporarily renamed (e.g., `*.disabled` extension) so it does not auto-activate.\\n3. Grade each output against the assertions list (pass/fail per assertion).\\n4. Produce a verdict report with: per-prompt scores, aggregate delta, suspected failure causes, recommended changes.\\n5. Restore the disabled artifact in a `finally` block AND register a recovery manifest at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/recovery.json` so a SIGKILL'd benchmark is restored on next `claude` invocation via a session-start hook.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| System | File/Path | Change Type | Risk |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Benchmark skill (new) | `plugins/development-harness/skills/benchmark/SKILL.md` | CREATE | High \u2014 primary deliverable; incorrect instructions mislead agents |\\n| Hooks registration | `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` | MODIFY | Medium \u2014 incorrect hook entry breaks SessionStart for all sessions |\\n| Session-start hook | `plugins/development-harness/hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` | REFERENCE (pattern copy) | Low \u2014 read-only pattern source |\\n| Benchmark state dir | `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/benchmark/` | CREATE (runtime) | Low \u2014 new directory; no existing consumers |\\n| Project-scope skills | `.claude/skills/` (project root) | ISOLATION CHECK | Low \u2014 must confirm benchmark skill does not shadow existing skills |\\n| Plugin skill registry | `~/.claude/plugins/cache/jamie-bitflight-skills/dh/*/skills/` | READ-ONLY | None \u2014 installed cache; changes in source tree only |\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d9940b959396930a4f841e5a095c5181edc344757bdc20476cf2f9fa16605c95\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnO5Rw\"}"}